WEBVTT

00:00:04.050 --> 00:00:06.720
That's a nice suit you've got on, sir.

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:09.850
I was in Milan until yesterday.

00:00:09.970 --> 00:00:12.560
Domenico tailored it especially for me.

00:00:12.640 --> 00:00:13.850
Wow.

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:15.810
I had to return home once I got there.

00:00:17.110 --> 00:00:20.650
Fate is finally on the move.

00:00:42.130 --> 00:00:43.670
<i>Hey! Quit dawdling!</i>

00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:47.180
Erm... Foxtrot mode... Foxtrot... Ack!

00:00:58.440 --> 00:01:00.690
How did she do, Captain Zaito?

00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:02.490
Hisone Amakasu.

00:01:03.150 --> 00:01:04.990
It's unthinkable.

00:01:05.150 --> 00:01:06.490
She lacks that much promise?

00:01:07.740 --> 00:01:09.080
She doesn't have the passion.

00:01:09.160 --> 00:01:09.990
What?

00:01:10.620 --> 00:01:11.660
For women,

00:01:12.330 --> 00:01:15.460
I'd welcome them
from the cradle to the grave!

00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:18.500
But Amakasu doesn't respond whatsoever!

00:01:19.790 --> 00:01:23.050
Ah, Flight Leader Kakiyasu,
she can do it.

00:01:23.170 --> 00:01:24.010
Do not worry!

00:01:25.300 --> 00:01:27.010
That does not put me at ease.

00:01:34.730 --> 00:01:36.020
Well done.

00:01:38.350 --> 00:01:39.400
Here! Eat up!

00:01:39.650 --> 00:01:41.320
K-Kaizaki...

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:44.360
You only chose Amakasu
for her flip phone, right?

00:01:44.440 --> 00:01:46.320
She sure is persistent.

00:01:46.650 --> 00:01:50.410
Come here and eat me! Eat me! Come on!

00:01:53.580 --> 00:01:54.950
He ate Kaizaki!

00:02:02.090 --> 00:02:03.840
The flip phones are gone...

00:02:03.960 --> 00:02:07.760
That's amazing.
You're quite nimble, aren't you?

00:02:09.510 --> 00:02:12.140
-How dare you mock me!
-Violence isn't the answer!

00:02:12.220 --> 00:02:14.140
Don't mess with me, you--

00:02:16.430 --> 00:02:17.270
I...

00:02:17.890 --> 00:02:19.230
Ikushima?

00:02:19.440 --> 00:02:21.230
You've come home!

00:02:21.310 --> 00:02:23.570
Finally, we meet.

00:02:24.110 --> 00:02:28.570
I... I really wanted to see you, too.

00:02:28.740 --> 00:02:32.280
But... I never thought
you'd say this here...

00:02:34.830 --> 00:02:35.660
Huh?

00:02:42.790 --> 00:02:45.210
Hips, 33.9 inches.

00:02:45.300 --> 00:02:48.970
I NAME THE DRAGON MASOTAN

00:03:10.030 --> 00:03:12.030
DRAGON PILOT: HISONE &amp; MASOTAN

00:04:32.570 --> 00:04:35.410
This man worked for Okamoto Kasei
and Barnes Wallis

00:04:35.490 --> 00:04:39.290
heading specialized clothing development.
This is Manager Ikushima.

00:04:39.370 --> 00:04:40.200
Mm-hmm.

00:04:40.580 --> 00:04:42.710
He develops pilots' suits?

00:04:42.790 --> 00:04:45.330
Well, the OTF suits

00:04:45.460 --> 00:04:48.090
are incomparable to other suits.

00:04:48.170 --> 00:04:52.800
First, they must not be dissolved
by gastric juices.

00:04:52.880 --> 00:04:57.640
Furthermore, they function as sensors
to check the organism and collect data.

00:04:57.930 --> 00:05:02.310
The OTF has been rejecting pilots
for three years.

00:05:02.470 --> 00:05:07.100
No matter what goodies we tried
to feed it, it wouldn't keep it in.

00:05:07.900 --> 00:05:11.820
But thanks to you,
we can rise to the next stage.

00:05:13.440 --> 00:05:15.450
Now then. Take off your clothes.

00:05:16.530 --> 00:05:18.120
I want you to relax.

00:05:18.950 --> 00:05:22.120
I'm only interested in your... body.

00:05:22.200 --> 00:05:24.160
A major problem is taking place!

00:05:24.250 --> 00:05:25.960
Shoulders, 14 inches.

00:05:27.830 --> 00:05:29.210
Mr. Ikushima!

00:05:29.630 --> 00:05:31.420
Oh, Kaizaki.

00:05:31.670 --> 00:05:35.630
I wrote a report on the prototype suit!

00:05:38.010 --> 00:05:41.390
Ask me anything!
I will cooperate to the fullest!

00:05:41.470 --> 00:05:42.640
I just have one question.

00:05:43.060 --> 00:05:46.020
Does Hisone Amakasu like sweet things?

00:05:46.100 --> 00:05:47.100
Huh?

00:05:47.190 --> 00:05:52.520
From what I could see, she's bordering
between a B-cup and a C-cup.

00:05:52.610 --> 00:05:54.610
Are you talking about Amakasu's suit?

00:05:55.030 --> 00:05:58.490
An extreme fluctuation in weight
will affect the measurements.

00:05:58.780 --> 00:05:59.780
Please excuse me.

00:06:02.080 --> 00:06:03.910
That bastard...

00:06:04.370 --> 00:06:06.040
I'm going to bully you to death!

00:06:06.370 --> 00:06:07.210
Achoo!

00:06:08.420 --> 00:06:09.830
Oh my.

00:06:11.040 --> 00:06:12.340
The mysterious Joa lady.

00:06:13.090 --> 00:06:15.880
Why do you always appear
when I'm troubled?

00:06:16.170 --> 00:06:18.380
Oh dear, you're feeling troubled?

00:06:18.550 --> 00:06:20.550
Oh! Um, yes.

00:06:20.840 --> 00:06:23.760
Well, I met someone recently.

00:06:25.350 --> 00:06:28.060
I felt like fate was calling me,

00:06:29.060 --> 00:06:32.480
like it saw something that only I have.

00:06:32.940 --> 00:06:34.820
Isn't that nice?

00:06:34.900 --> 00:06:36.820
But now that I've started,

00:06:36.900 --> 00:06:40.610
it's not going well, and I'm full of
bewilderment, hardship, and distress.

00:06:40.700 --> 00:06:43.620
And then this very forward
pervert appeared...

00:06:44.410 --> 00:06:45.370
Here.

00:06:45.450 --> 00:06:48.540
Have a yogurt.

00:06:48.620 --> 00:06:49.620
Thank you very--

00:06:53.960 --> 00:06:57.920
That lady works in mysterious ways.
There must be some meaning attached.

00:06:59.550 --> 00:07:00.840
I don't have a spoon.

00:07:04.510 --> 00:07:06.520
Ground beef cutlet today, huh?

00:07:08.100 --> 00:07:09.980
You eat this one.

00:07:11.310 --> 00:07:16.020
<i>You're undeserving of this super delicious</i>
<i>ground beef cutlet, newbie.</i>

00:07:16.150 --> 00:07:18.780
<i>You're only worthy of</i>
<i>this crappy croquette I made.</i>

00:07:20.360 --> 00:07:24.530
The potatoes are so chunky,
they roll in my mouth. It's so yummy!

00:07:32.880 --> 00:07:34.670
<i>Try sleeping through this.</i>

00:07:35.130 --> 00:07:38.800
<i>You'll be too tired to function tomorrow!</i>

00:07:39.090 --> 00:07:41.970
Lakitu, Lakitu...

00:07:42.550 --> 00:07:45.510
Goro loved that character...

00:07:45.640 --> 00:07:48.270
Imagine being on that cloud...

00:07:52.690 --> 00:07:54.190
How is she sleeping?!

00:07:54.270 --> 00:07:55.810
The nerve of this nitwit...

00:08:06.240 --> 00:08:08.330
I'm so hooked on the story, I can't sleep.

00:08:11.410 --> 00:08:12.370
I slept like a baby!

00:08:12.870 --> 00:08:15.210
Oh, good morning!

00:08:16.460 --> 00:08:19.250
Kaizaki, you've got some
dark circles under your eyes.

00:08:19.420 --> 00:08:20.380
Shuddap!

00:08:22.090 --> 00:08:24.180
You forgot to gargle!

00:08:27.100 --> 00:08:31.180
<i>Kaizaki might act like</i>
<i>she's in a bad mood, but I know better.</i>

00:08:31.350 --> 00:08:35.060
<i>She gave me her croquette so I didn't have</i>
<i>to eat ground meat I don't like.</i>

00:08:35.230 --> 00:08:38.110
<i>She cheered me up</i>
<i>so I wouldn't feel homesick.</i>

00:08:38.190 --> 00:08:41.190
<i>She's actually a kind and mature woman.</i>

00:08:41.440 --> 00:08:42.490
Kaizaki...

00:08:42.570 --> 00:08:45.360
no, maybe I'll call her Nao next time.

00:08:45.530 --> 00:08:48.580
A stable position in the body
directly after being swallowed

00:08:48.660 --> 00:08:53.620
greatly affects the reaction speed of the
following Action Control Signal, or ACS.

00:08:53.710 --> 00:08:54.920
Onto action coordinates.

00:08:55.000 --> 00:08:57.330
-Nao. Nao!
-All positions start with actions...

00:08:57.670 --> 00:09:00.460
Hey! Who gave you permission
to be casual with me?!

00:09:00.550 --> 00:09:02.050
-You--
-Third Class Kaizaki.

00:09:09.350 --> 00:09:13.770
I understand the arrival of a new Dragon
Pilot prospect can divert your attention.

00:09:13.850 --> 00:09:14.690
However,

00:09:15.390 --> 00:09:20.190
what would Former Officer Kaizaki
think of your carefree attitude?

00:09:23.320 --> 00:09:24.780
Now then, continuing on.

00:09:27.780 --> 00:09:29.700
Wow, a lot is coming off of you!

00:09:29.990 --> 00:09:32.490
It's because it's very humid here.

00:09:32.580 --> 00:09:35.830
Every three days we need
to wash off the red mold.

00:09:36.210 --> 00:09:39.080
You look like you're
enjoying yourself, Mr. OTF.

00:09:39.170 --> 00:09:42.590
Come to think of it,
what is Mr. OTF's name?

00:09:42.670 --> 00:09:45.260
Can't he just be F-15J?

00:09:45.340 --> 00:09:47.470
That's just the name of his armor.

00:09:47.760 --> 00:09:52.640
-It's like calling me "work uniform."
-I see what you mean.

00:09:53.020 --> 00:09:55.270
What about Otofu?

00:09:55.600 --> 00:09:56.600
"Otofu?"

00:09:56.890 --> 00:09:57.770
Said like that?

00:09:58.020 --> 00:09:59.900
Don't you get it?

00:10:00.110 --> 00:10:01.610
OTF.

00:10:01.980 --> 00:10:04.030
OTF. Oh-to-fu.

00:10:04.150 --> 00:10:06.360
Oh tofu. Otofu!

00:10:06.450 --> 00:10:07.280
Like that!

00:10:07.610 --> 00:10:10.070
No I mean, I got that part...

00:10:10.160 --> 00:10:13.790
Speaking of names,
who is Former Officer Kaizaki?

00:10:14.080 --> 00:10:16.910
Oh, I believe that's Kaizaki's mother.

00:10:17.330 --> 00:10:20.170
Huh? Is being a Dragon Pilot hereditary?

00:10:20.290 --> 00:10:22.170
No, that's not it.

00:10:22.380 --> 00:10:24.250
But before you came,

00:10:24.340 --> 00:10:27.630
Kaizaki was the leading
Dragon Pilot candidate.

00:10:28.010 --> 00:10:29.680
Before I came?

00:10:30.010 --> 00:10:34.720
Yes. Commander Sosoda and Flight Leader
Kakiyasu had high hopes for her--

00:10:37.020 --> 00:10:38.310
Ah, I'm sorry!

00:10:38.730 --> 00:10:40.400
You shouldn't feel burdened--

00:10:40.480 --> 00:10:42.480
What a truly amazing person she is,

00:10:42.690 --> 00:10:43.520
Nao!

00:10:44.860 --> 00:10:47.280
Normally, I wouldn't think it's possible!

00:10:47.360 --> 00:10:50.740
But to think that she extended a hand
to a rival who destroyed her dreams!

00:10:51.530 --> 00:10:53.700
I... I...

00:10:54.530 --> 00:10:55.580
Ah!

00:10:58.410 --> 00:10:59.500
Yogurt?

00:10:59.870 --> 00:11:02.500
Yeah! It's been in my pocket
since yesterday.

00:11:02.580 --> 00:11:03.420
Yech...

00:11:03.670 --> 00:11:06.670
And I've just realized
something extraordinary!

00:11:07.130 --> 00:11:11.890
The Joa lady was using this yogurt's
catchphrase to tell me to root for Nao!

00:11:12.220 --> 00:11:16.930
I shall support the stomach.
Nay, I shall support Nao!

00:11:17.020 --> 00:11:20.480
W-What the hell is she saying?

00:11:20.890 --> 00:11:23.400
That's why I'm sorry, Otofu,

00:11:23.480 --> 00:11:26.400
but could you let Nao
ride you instead of me?

00:11:27.440 --> 00:11:29.570
-A-Amakasu...
-It'll be great!

00:11:29.650 --> 00:11:31.820
Nao may look like a child,

00:11:31.910 --> 00:11:33.570
-Um...
-but she acts her age,

00:11:33.910 --> 00:11:35.830
and she has good judgment!

00:11:36.160 --> 00:11:39.500
On top of that, I'm not as eager
to be a Dragon Pilot.

00:11:39.660 --> 00:11:41.670
You'll see that she's a kind person.

00:11:41.750 --> 00:11:44.840
And you shouldn't judge a person
before you eat her, Otofu!

00:11:44.920 --> 00:11:47.420
Amakasu! I think
that's unnecessary to say...

00:11:51.970 --> 00:11:53.970
I don't need your damn charity!

00:11:57.260 --> 00:12:01.390
You... half-assed wench!

00:12:05.230 --> 00:12:08.070
Oh no... did Nao hear everything?!

00:12:08.530 --> 00:12:09.570
Otofu!

00:12:09.650 --> 00:12:11.530
What should I do?!

00:12:18.910 --> 00:12:20.830
Wait, Otofu!

00:12:21.750 --> 00:12:24.250
Otofu!

00:12:28.840 --> 00:12:30.210
U-Um...

00:12:34.550 --> 00:12:36.800
I shouldn't talk to her.

00:12:36.890 --> 00:12:39.510
My frankness only hurts people.

00:12:39.600 --> 00:12:43.230
I can't mimic the same kind of attack
on Nao after hurting her.

00:12:43.440 --> 00:12:48.150
We'll both calm down after a night
and Nao's stance should soften.

00:12:49.070 --> 00:12:52.150
<i>Why do I have to be calm?!</i>

00:12:52.280 --> 00:12:55.280
<i>The only one who's gonna calm down</i>
<i>is you, dumbass.</i>

00:12:57.200 --> 00:12:58.700
<i>Heh heh, time to cut it.</i>

00:12:59.030 --> 00:13:00.910
<i>Snip. Shock!</i>

00:13:02.370 --> 00:13:05.920
<i>Ah, I can't dance anymore.</i>

00:13:07.040 --> 00:13:08.920
I've got it.

00:13:09.000 --> 00:13:13.720
Hiso Maso!

00:13:15.680 --> 00:13:19.390
Now then, shall we begin
viewing the suit fittings?

00:13:26.190 --> 00:13:27.400
Oh.

00:13:27.770 --> 00:13:28.650
<i>Bon.</i>

00:13:28.900 --> 00:13:29.980
<i>Tres bien.</i>

00:13:30.190 --> 00:13:31.150
<i>Wunderbar.</i>

00:13:33.360 --> 00:13:36.530
What do you call
this kind of shaming for fun?

00:13:36.610 --> 00:13:41.620
I've taken fantasy into reality
from head to toe on Hisone's body.

00:13:41.790 --> 00:13:45.040
Please, enough with
the unpleasant visceral expressions!

00:13:45.120 --> 00:13:46.580
Looking good, Amakasu.

00:13:46.710 --> 00:13:48.920
Everything looks good on you, doesn't it?

00:13:49.000 --> 00:13:50.290
Commander Sosoda now, too?!

00:13:50.840 --> 00:13:53.130
Try on the next suit.

00:13:53.960 --> 00:13:57.720
Now then, let's have you
board the OTF so we may collect data.

00:13:57.800 --> 00:14:00.680
Do I really have to wear this suit?

00:14:16.440 --> 00:14:18.030
What are you doing?

00:14:18.450 --> 00:14:20.410
Oh, um, nothing.

00:14:27.750 --> 00:14:30.040
Hand it over, 3rd Class Kaizaki.

00:14:36.550 --> 00:14:40.260
Doing this will only make you miserable.

00:14:41.010 --> 00:14:42.800
If it were Former Officer Kaizaki,

00:14:42.890 --> 00:14:44.430
she would be fair and graceful--

00:14:44.510 --> 00:14:46.520
Please stop saying Mama's name.

00:14:47.520 --> 00:14:50.350
If you've got a problem,
we can rotate you.

00:14:50.440 --> 00:14:51.810
You can request it anytime.

00:14:55.360 --> 00:14:56.530
I quit.

00:14:57.400 --> 00:15:00.160
I quit the Gifu Air Base!

00:15:04.280 --> 00:15:06.450
Don't be so down about it!

00:15:06.620 --> 00:15:09.410
We aren't men without
our hunting instinct!

00:15:09.830 --> 00:15:11.250
It's my pride.

00:15:11.420 --> 00:15:13.290
-If a woman cooks well--
-Huh?

00:15:15.170 --> 00:15:16.880
Oh, Nao!

00:15:16.960 --> 00:15:18.880
Are you finally running into my arms--

00:15:20.510 --> 00:15:21.590
-Eh?
-Hey!

00:15:21.680 --> 00:15:22.550
Hey, wait!

00:15:23.970 --> 00:15:25.850
My bike!

00:15:28.600 --> 00:15:30.600
Nao's gone off the rails!

00:15:33.270 --> 00:15:37.280
<i>It turns out that Nao</i>
<i>left on the bike she stole,</i>

00:15:37.570 --> 00:15:40.900
<i>and didn't even come back</i>
<i>the following night.</i>

00:15:41.820 --> 00:15:44.370
<i>The number you are trying to reach</i>
<i>is unavailable.</i>

00:15:44.700 --> 00:15:46.410
-A deserter, eh?
-My bike...

00:15:46.490 --> 00:15:47.370
What a problem.

00:15:47.790 --> 00:15:51.160
This is why we've got a problem with
the all-women Dragon Pilots.

00:15:51.620 --> 00:15:54.420
They do as they please.
We're sick of cleaning up after them!

00:15:54.960 --> 00:15:56.210
My deepest apologies.

00:15:56.630 --> 00:15:59.090
But I wonder if she'll be okay?

00:15:59.670 --> 00:16:02.470
She doesn't seem
like she has a fat wallet.

00:16:02.590 --> 00:16:03.680
Wallet?

00:16:03.970 --> 00:16:06.760
A search party costs about a million.

00:16:06.890 --> 00:16:10.180
The fee comes out
of the deserter's pocket of course.

00:16:10.270 --> 00:16:13.690
Nao will be in that much debt
at such a young age?

00:16:14.270 --> 00:16:16.770
What if she gets fired
from the Air Self-Defense Force?

00:16:16.860 --> 00:16:18.940
She'd need a night job that pays well,

00:16:19.030 --> 00:16:22.530
but with her childish looks,
she'd need to falsify her record.

00:16:22.610 --> 00:16:24.570
-But before that...
-She talking to herself?

00:16:24.660 --> 00:16:27.620
-We can hear it all.
-Isn't she saying some terrible things?

00:16:27.700 --> 00:16:28.990
You're one to talk.

00:16:29.080 --> 00:16:30.620
Let me say one more thing!

00:16:31.200 --> 00:16:36.000
Let me and OTF Otofu take over
the search for Nao!

00:16:37.380 --> 00:16:39.340
If we do that, it won't cost any money.

00:16:39.420 --> 00:16:42.720
And you think you can so easily
maneuver the OTF to fly?!

00:16:43.630 --> 00:16:46.970
What if we deploy it tonight in the dark?

00:16:47.300 --> 00:16:48.810
Commander Sosoda!

00:16:49.010 --> 00:16:50.470
Thank you very much!

00:16:54.140 --> 00:16:55.480
-Oh.
-Mr. Ikushima!

00:16:55.770 --> 00:16:56.900
Oh, Hisone.

00:16:57.270 --> 00:16:59.980
-You know, I'm satisfied with--
-Is that a suit?!

00:17:02.820 --> 00:17:03.990
I'm borrowing this.

00:17:05.610 --> 00:17:07.620
So she picked that suit.

00:17:07.910 --> 00:17:09.280
That's just like her.

00:17:09.700 --> 00:17:10.990
Nice sense.

00:17:11.580 --> 00:17:12.750
Otofu!

00:17:13.250 --> 00:17:14.250
Hm? Ah!

00:17:14.410 --> 00:17:17.630
Amakasu... your suit...

00:17:18.710 --> 00:17:21.590
All right, Otofu. Hurry up and swallow me!

00:17:23.720 --> 00:17:24.630
What's wrong?

00:17:25.220 --> 00:17:26.930
I want to find Nao!

00:17:27.220 --> 00:17:28.260
Please.

00:17:31.640 --> 00:17:32.470
Huh?

00:17:40.940 --> 00:17:42.030
I wonder if

00:17:42.780 --> 00:17:44.320
Otofu and Nao

00:17:44.990 --> 00:17:46.280
share the same feelings?

00:17:49.280 --> 00:17:50.280
I'm sorry!

00:17:50.740 --> 00:17:53.620
If I'm asked if I want to be
a Dragon Pilot,

00:17:53.790 --> 00:17:56.870
I still don't actively and passionately
feel that I want to.

00:17:56.960 --> 00:17:59.750
You're supposed to lie and say you do...

00:17:59.880 --> 00:18:05.720
But I do believe I found
something only I can do!

00:18:06.220 --> 00:18:07.220
I apologize!

00:18:07.470 --> 00:18:09.890
Please forgive my half-witted remarks!

00:18:10.720 --> 00:18:12.260
And please,

00:18:12.350 --> 00:18:14.640
grant my wish, Otofu!

00:18:16.520 --> 00:18:18.440
Otofu!

00:18:23.780 --> 00:18:25.440
<i>Mambo Viking 01.</i>

00:18:26.110 --> 00:18:28.950
<i>Wind 090 at 7.</i>

00:18:29.070 --> 00:18:31.910
<i>Runway 28 cleared for takeoff.</i>

00:18:32.280 --> 00:18:34.830
C-Cleared for takeoff.

00:18:40.580 --> 00:18:43.130
Ma... so... tan?

00:18:44.960 --> 00:18:48.050
By chance, is your name Masotan?

00:18:54.600 --> 00:18:55.770
I see.

00:18:55.890 --> 00:18:56.720
Well then.

00:18:56.810 --> 00:18:58.600
Let's go, Masotan!

00:18:58.890 --> 00:19:00.100
Let's go find Nao!

00:19:19.660 --> 00:19:23.170
I say that, but how are we gonna find her?

00:19:28.800 --> 00:19:30.430
M-Masotan!

00:19:42.810 --> 00:19:45.610
It hurts! Someone help me please...

00:19:46.320 --> 00:19:47.360
Mama...

00:20:07.880 --> 00:20:10.050
We're here to take you home, Nao.

00:20:11.380 --> 00:20:13.300
You're... injured!

00:20:14.430 --> 00:20:15.850
It's just a scratch.

00:20:16.550 --> 00:20:20.180
Masotan, sorry, but could you take Nao?

00:20:20.270 --> 00:20:21.520
Masotan?

00:20:21.940 --> 00:20:25.940
The base is nearby so at this distance,
you won't melt without a suit.

00:20:27.520 --> 00:20:28.400
I can't.

00:20:28.480 --> 00:20:30.190
It'll be okay.

00:20:30.320 --> 00:20:32.650
-I can just walk--
-That's not it!

00:20:36.320 --> 00:20:38.870
He won't swallow me up.

00:20:38.950 --> 00:20:40.660
That's not true.

00:20:40.910 --> 00:20:44.420
Masotan remembers your scent.

00:20:44.580 --> 00:20:46.380
That's how we found you.

00:20:46.830 --> 00:20:47.960
This guy did?

00:20:49.710 --> 00:20:51.260
It's not "this guy."

00:20:51.340 --> 00:20:52.720
Masotan.

00:20:54.720 --> 00:20:56.720
Masotan--

00:21:09.270 --> 00:21:11.480
Thank you, Masotan.

00:21:19.450 --> 00:21:23.450
As an exception, your report
will be taken care of externally.

00:21:23.750 --> 00:21:24.580
Huh?

00:21:24.750 --> 00:21:27.460
You know too much about the OTF.

00:21:27.540 --> 00:21:29.540
I will not allow you
to quit the flight team.

00:21:29.630 --> 00:21:30.880
-But--
-If you want to quit,

00:21:30.960 --> 00:21:34.050
you will pay the million yen fee
for the search party.

00:21:34.130 --> 00:21:35.430
Wait just a minute!

00:21:35.510 --> 00:21:37.470
Does that mean I can stay...

00:21:37.550 --> 00:21:40.600
In the future, we will need
many Dragon Pilots.

00:21:40.680 --> 00:21:45.440
You have cleared the first condition
requiring you to be swallowed by an OTF.

00:21:46.230 --> 00:21:49.900
You are an excellent candidate
to become a Dragon Pilot,

00:21:50.230 --> 00:21:51.270
Third Class Kaizaki.

00:21:53.230 --> 00:21:55.110
I understand how you feel.

00:21:55.990 --> 00:21:58.660
I was just like you a long time ago.

00:21:59.660 --> 00:22:00.700
Work hard.

00:22:02.240 --> 00:22:03.080
Yes, ma'am!

00:22:03.910 --> 00:22:04.830
Please excuse me!

00:22:06.620 --> 00:22:08.000
Woosh!

00:22:08.080 --> 00:22:09.210
Veer!

00:22:09.290 --> 00:22:10.790
Pew pew pew!

00:22:11.590 --> 00:22:12.420
Oh!

00:22:12.550 --> 00:22:13.920
Fire!

00:22:14.090 --> 00:22:16.380
M-Masotan! Hang in there!

00:22:16.470 --> 00:22:19.220
If you don't want that to be your fate,
then you gotta train!

00:22:19.800 --> 00:22:20.640
You got it!

00:22:21.050 --> 00:22:22.600
Is that so?

00:22:22.760 --> 00:22:26.230
Hisone Amakasu calls her OTF Masotan?

00:22:26.640 --> 00:22:27.480
Yes, sir.

00:22:28.560 --> 00:22:31.360
Calling an OTF by its true name...

00:22:31.940 --> 00:22:34.730
As I thought, she is

00:22:34.820 --> 00:22:36.650
the chosen <i>Miko.</i>

00:22:36.740 --> 00:22:38.950
TO BE CONTINUED

00:24:09.750 --> 00:24:12.250
You said you'd do it,
so take responsibility!

00:24:12.330 --> 00:24:14.460
Take responsibility, huh?

00:24:14.540 --> 00:24:16.340
Mine should be hard.

00:24:16.420 --> 00:24:18.300
Oh! Not there!

00:24:21.300 --> 00:24:22.340
Sweet.
